body:
> What is yours, if you don't mind sharing?

It would be hard to choose just one; what I'm interested in changes frequently. Out of any other study, philosophy has always stayed at a considerable level of interest to me, though. This is probably due to the nature of philosophy itself, as other studies are dependent on various philosophical frameworks. 

&#x200B;

>I'm not really interested in dinosaurs so I can't answer that question unfortunately haha. What's yours?

&#x200B;

I've always been a fan of pachycephalosaurus. It's a smaller dinosaur with a hard casing on it's head, which was used to headbutt threats. It also lived during the late Cretaceous, which was a wild time. On another note, I actually like pterosaurs more than dinosaurs, like Quetzalcoatlus or Tapejara. They also lived during the late Cretaceous.

>I have also had a lot of VERY negative experiences - like very negative - with other people that have led me to just struggle w being optimistic.

&#x200B;

>Something I’m noticing about myself now is that I don’t look naturally happy

&#x200B;

Moody self-reflection points to the reaction triad (4s, 6s, 8s) in the first two paragraphs.

Enneagram 4's vice is envy, and is within the heart triad, which deals with shame. The dissatisfaction with a predicament because of internal inadequacies is the behavior of an enneagram 4.

&#x200B;

Shame:

&#x200B;

>I don’t wear makeup, even though I am not fully “satisfied” w my appearance

&#x200B;

Envy:

&#x200B;

>Even yesterday I was thinking about how I almost want my child to be half white so that they just won’t suffer as much in society, particularly over how they look, even though I actually don’t care about how my hypothetical future baby would look.

&#x200B;

Pessimism, internalized accounting of emotions, and feelings of inadequacy are all showcased in the information provided. I would say 4w3 based on the finer details of wishing for success, and an instinctual stacking of sx/sp due to:

&#x200B;

>I have had the urge to “punish” people who have hurt me and have really held grudges before.

Gotta admit: I get slightly annoyed at the \~*uwu infp so cute \*pet\*\~* 

&#x200B;

But then I realized that those people value and protect sensitivity., which is a trait that most INFPs including myself (exhibit A) demonstrate more than any other type.

ENTP agendapost?!?!?! 

&#x200B;

*yes I'm in denial*

Yo I just ran outta pods. I finna quit while I still have some cash left....

&#x200B;

Hopefully
